#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""hotseat-indicator: Hotseat's menu bar app for Linux (GNOME on X11).

A port of macos/Sources/Hotseat (AppDelegate, AccountCard, SettingsView,
SetupView): a top-bar icon whose menu has one card per account, plus
Settings…, Setup…, Refresh and Quit; a Settings window (Accounts, General)
and a Setup window with the same steps and wording as the Mac app.

Like the Mac app it only displays and clicks: everything is read from
`hotseat panel --json` / `hotseat setup status --json`, and every action
runs the `hotseat` CLI. It makes no network requests and reads none of
Claude's files.

Needs only GTK 3 and PyGObject (stock on Ubuntu). The icon is a legacy tray
icon (Gtk.StatusIcon), which Ubuntu's AppIndicator extension shows in the
top bar on X11 sessions.

Differences from the Mac app, all forced by the platform: no text beside the
icon (a tray icon is a square image; the tooltip carries it), shortcuts are
Ctrl+key while the menu is open, account icons are emoji instead of SF
Symbols, and there is no bundled CLI to install (Setup's first step only
checks ~/.local/bin/hotseat).

SIGUSR1 toggles the menu (to open it from a script or over SSH).
"""
